# Shareland Exchange - Project Overview

## What Is Shareland

Shareland is a tokenized real estate exchange platform. Users can buy, sell, and trade fractional ownership of real estate properties represented as on-chain tokens. The platform includes:

- A web-based trading interface (React frontend)
- A REST API with real-time data processing (Express/Prisma backend)
- Smart contracts for on-chain market mechanics (Solidity/Hardhat)
- Public documentation site (Mintlify)

## Repository Structure

Eight active repositories live in this workspace. Each belongs to one of three **ticket flows** (defined in `ticket-management.mdc`) which decide how work ships and which project-board columns apply. Check the flow before assuming anything about releases or testnet.

| Repo | Purpose | How it deploys | Flow |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shareland-react` | Exchange front-end (share.land) | GitHub Actions on GitHub Release: **prerelease → testnet, release → mainnet** | Exchange stack |
| `shareland-api` | REST API, Prisma/Postgres | GitHub Release: **prerelease → staging, release → production**, building a Docker image to ECR. `workflow_dispatch` also available | Exchange stack |
| `shareland-contracts` | Solidity contracts on Base | Operator-run Hardhat scripts, no CI/CD trail | Exchange stack |
| `shareland-daemons` | Oracle, statistics, notification daemons | Manual `workflow_dispatch` to ECR then ECS | Exchange stack |
| `shareland-common` | Shared types, formulas, utilities | Published to GitHub Package Registry, then consumers bump | Deploy after merge |
| `shareland-docs` | Public docs (docs.share.land) | Mintlify auto-deploys on merge to `main` | Deploy on merge |
| `shareland-mission-control` | Internal ops and KPI dashboard | Vercel auto-deploys on merge to `main` | Deploy on merge |
| `shareland-prototypes` | Agentic prototyping sandbox | Vercel auto-deploys on merge to `main` | Deploy on merge |

`shareland-cities-lp` is also checked out in the workspace but is **archived on GitHub** and read-only. Do not open issues or PRs against it.

Note that `shareland-daemons` uses **`master`** as its default branch. Every other repo uses `main`.

**Only the exchange stack** — react, api, contracts, daemons — has a testnet (Base Sepolia, testnet.share.land). The deploy-on-merge repos have no testnet and no releases: the merge *is* the deploy.

Also in the org but outside this workspace: `shareland-webapp` (the pre-split monorepo, kept for reference only), `dev-tools`, `open-graph-scraper`, `trading-view-charting`. Ten dead repos were archived in July 2026.

### shareland-react (Frontend)
- **Tech**: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Radix UI
- **Auth**: Privy (Web3Auth) with wagmi for wallet interactions
- **State**: TanStack React Query for server state
- **i18n**: i18next with 6 locales (en, zh-CN, de, es, fr, hi)
- **Testing**: Cypress for e2e tests, Storybook for component dev
- **Analytics**: Amplitude
- **Maps**: Mapbox GL
- **Charts**: Recharts, TradingView charting library
- **Package manager**: npm
- **Lint/Format**: ESLint + Prettier (run `npm run format` then `npm run lint`)

### shareland-api (API)
- **Tech**: Express.js, TypeScript, Prisma ORM, PostgreSQL
- **Runtime**: Bun
- **Deploy**: `api-build-docker.yml` on a full GitHub Release (production) and `api-staging-build-docker.yml` on a prerelease or draft (staging). Both also accept a manual `workflow_dispatch`.
- **Auth**: Privy server-auth, Web3Auth signature verification
- **Blockchain**: ethers.js, viem for contract interactions
- **Services**: Sentry (error tracking), AWS S3, Resend (email), Google Sheets
- **Daemons**: Statistics daemon, Oracle daemon, Database notifications daemon
- **Package manager**: bun
- **Lint/Format**: ESLint + Prettier (run `bun run format` then `bun run lint`)

### shareland-contracts (Smart Contracts)
- **Tech**: Solidity, Hardhat, OpenZeppelin (upgradeable contracts)
- **Key contracts**: ShareLandMarket, ShareLandToken, OrderBook, LiquidityProviderToken, CollateralPosition
- **Testing**: Hardhat test with Chai matchers
- **Runtime**: Bun
- **Networks**: Base mainnet, Base Sepolia (testnet)
- **Lint/Format**: ESLint + Prettier + solhint (run `bun run format` then `bun run lint`)

### shareland-docs (Documentation)
- **Tech**: Mintlify, MDX
- **URL**: https://docs.share.land
- **Structure**: `guides/` (getting started), `how-to/` (user guides), `reference/` (FAQ, glossary, contracts)
- **Config**: `docs.json` defines navigation, theme, and branding
- **Deployment**: Mintlify auto-deploys on push to `main`
- **Images**: `/images/screenshots/` for UI screenshots

### shareland-common (Shared Library)
- **Tech**: TypeScript, Rollup (bundler)
- **Runtime**: Bun
- **Exports**: Shared types, market formula JS implementations, utility functions
- **Key exports**: `getLandPortfolioValue`, `MarketFormulaJS`, `decimalsMultiplier`, shared types
- **Published as**: `@shareland/shareland-common` on GitHub Package Registry
- **Depends on**: `@shareland/shareland-contracts`, `viem`, `decimal.js`, `ethers`
- **Build**: `bun install && bun run build` (output in `dist/`)
- **Lint/Format**: ESLint + Prettier (run `bun run validate`)

### shareland-daemons (Background Workers)
- **Tech**: TypeScript, Bun
- **Workers**: Oracle price updater, statistics daemon, database notification daemon
- **Deploy**: `daemon-deploy-ecr.yml` then `daemon-deploy-ecs.yml`, both manual `workflow_dispatch`
- **Lint/Format**: `bun run format` then `bun run lint`
- **Note**: Oracle and statistics work belongs here, **not** in `shareland-api`

### shareland-mission-control (Internal Dashboard)
- **Tech**: Next.js, TypeScript, npm
- **Purpose**: Internal ops, KPI and goal-board dashboard. Not user-facing.
- **Deploy**: Vercel, auto-deploys on merge to `main`
- **Checks**: `npm run build`, then `npm run test:verify` (data and KPI verification suite)
- **Note**: PRs are recommended to avoid collisions, not enforced. Has its own `.cursor/rules/` covering repo scope and its ticket flow.

### shareland-prototypes (Sandbox)
- **Tech**: Next.js, TypeScript, npm
- **Purpose**: Agentic prototyping. Holds multiple independent prototypes side by side (e.g. gifting, exchange-redesign).
- **Deploy**: Vercel, auto-deploys on merge to `main`
- **Note**: Not production. PRs recommended when more than one person or agent is working in it.

## Shared Dependencies

- `@shareland/shareland-contracts` - NPM package consumed by frontend, API, and common
- `@shareland/shareland-common` - Shared types, utilities, and formulas (e.g., `getLandPortfolioValue`, `MarketFormulaJS`)
- Both frontend and API use `viem` for blockchain interactions
- All `@shareland/*` packages are published to **GitHub Package Registry** (`https://npm.pkg.github.com`)

### GitHub Packages Authentication

All `@shareland/*` packages require auth to install. The registry and token are configured via `.npmrc`:

```ini
@shareland:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<GITHUB_PAT_WITH_READ_PACKAGES>
```

**Where this lives:**
- **User-level** `~/.npmrc` (i.e., `C:\Users\<user>\.npmrc` on Windows, `~/.npmrc` on macOS) — applies globally to all repos
- **Repo-level** `.npmrc` — some repos (e.g., `shareland-api`) also have a local copy

**If `bun install` or `npm install` returns 401 for `@shareland/*`:**
1. Check that `~/.npmrc` exists and contains the lines above
2. If using **bun**, it may not read user-level `.npmrc` — copy `~/.npmrc` into the repo root (but do NOT commit the token; ensure `.gitignore` excludes `.npmrc`)
3. If the token is expired, generate a new classic PAT at https://github.com/settings/tokens with `read:packages` scope

### Working on shareland-common Locally

The `shareland-common` repo lives at `shareland-exchange/shareland-common` in the workspace.

**Build:**
```bash
cd shareland-common
bun install   # requires GitHub Packages auth (see above)
bun run build
```

**Test changes in shareland-react without publishing:**
```bash
# In shareland-react:
npm run use-local-common   # switches dep to file:../shareland-common
# ... test your changes ...
npm run restore-common     # reverts to registry version before committing
```

**Publish a new version:**
1. Bump version in `shareland-common/package.json`
2. Build: `bun run build`
3. Publish: `npm publish` (requires a PAT with `write:packages`)
4. Bump `@shareland/shareland-common` version in `shareland-react/package.json` and `shareland-api/package.json`

## Key Conventions

- All repos use absolute imports (no relative paths in frontend; use `#/` prefix)
- All repos enforce zero ESLint warnings (`--max-warnings 0`)
- Frontend uses Tailwind CSS with mobile-first responsive design
- API uses Prisma for all database access
- Smart contracts use OpenZeppelin upgradeable patterns with beacon proxies

## Cursor Rules & Skills Infrastructure

### Architecture (as of 2026-02-13)

Rules and skills live **directly in each repo** under `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/`. There is NO submodule, NO external repo, and NO shared monorepo for Cursor configuration.

**IMPORTANT:** The `shareland-cursor` repo was deleted. Do NOT reference it, create it, or propose submodules. The current approach is direct file copies.

### Org-wide rules (synced to all eight active workspace repos)

These 5 rules exist in `shareland-react`, `shareland-api`, `shareland-contracts`, `shareland-daemons`, `shareland-common`, `shareland-docs`, `shareland-mission-control` and `shareland-prototypes`:
- `pr-workflow.mdc` — PR conventions, branch naming, per-repo checks, exchange-stack releases, `Relates to` (NOT `Closes`)
- `planning-workflow.mdc` — Plan before implementing multi-file changes
- `project-overview.mdc` — This file
- `ticket-management.mdc` — Ticket flows, GitHub Issues, project board field IDs, status/priority/size options
- `shell-environment.mdc` — Windows/PowerShell compatibility

`shareland-cities-lp` is archived and deliberately excluded.

### Repo-specific rules
- `frontend-conventions.mdc` — Only in `shareland-react`
- `api-conventions.mdc` — Only in `shareland-api`
- `mission-control.mdc`, `mission-control-scope.mdc`, `mission-control-tickets.mdc` — Only in `shareland-mission-control`

**Precedence:** where a repo-specific rule and an org-wide rule disagree, the repo-specific rule wins for that repo. `mission-control-tickets.mdc` is the live example — it closes issues at deploy, where the org rule closes only after verification.

### Skills per repo
- **shareland-react:** cypress-testing, i18n-translations, pre-commit-checks, responsive-design, self-code-review, small-branch-planning
- **shareland-api:** pre-commit-checks (bun-adapted), self-code-review, small-branch-planning
- **shareland-contracts:** pre-commit-checks (bun/hardhat-adapted), self-code-review, small-branch-planning
- **shareland-mission-control:** mission-control-ship
- **shareland-daemons, shareland-common, shareland-docs, shareland-prototypes:** none yet

### Changing org-wide rules

The workspace-root `.cursor/rules/` is the **editing surface**, but it is not under version control — it is one person's multi-root workspace config. **Authority lives in the repos**: whatever is on `main` in each repo is what agents working there actually load. Keep the two aligned.

1. Edit the copy in the workspace root `.cursor/rules/`
2. Run `.\scripts\sync-org-rules.ps1 -Check` to see which repos differ from it, compared against `origin/main` rather than whatever branch happens to be checked out
3. Run `.\scripts\sync-org-rules.ps1 -Apply` to stage the change. It builds each commit in a throwaway worktree off `origin/main`, so it can never inject a rules chore into someone's open feature branch
4. Push the branches it created and open one PR per repo (direct push to `main` is fine for the deploy-on-merge repos)

If you are in a single-repo window and cannot reach the workspace root, edit the rule in your repo, say so in the PR body, and ask for it to be propagated.

### Intent tracking

The project manager agent maintains `.cursor/plans/INTENTS.md` in the workspace root. This tracks all active work streams, PR statuses, and board state. Agents in repo-scoped windows won't see this file directly — use copy/paste for handoff.

